Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 22:38:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 032/143] drm/sun4i: sun55i_de: layer_update filters by LOGICAL
 channel (7.1 vs 6.18 drift)

On 6.18 the sun8i_layer carries a logical channel (vi_num+index; primary
UI=1) and the mapping to physical is done by map[] when computing bases. The
patch (written against 7.1, where the channel is already physical) compared
against physical 6, so layer_update returned early for ALL planes: the RCQ
pool never contained the plane OVL/BLD and every RCQ load overwrote with
zeros what the MMIO path had painted (the fbcon penguins were visible until
the first arm erased them -> green background screen).
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
index 08f0180f0..0594a97d3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
@@ -749,9 +749,14 @@ void sun55i_de_layer_update(struct sun8i_mixer *mixer, struct sun8i_layer *layer
 	dma_addr_t addr;
 	u32 fmt, attctl;
 
-	/* this milestone only drives the first UI channel (phys 6) */
+	/*
+	 * this milestone only drives the first UI channel (logic 1 = phys 6).
+	 * On 6.18 layer->channel is the LOGICAL channel (vi_num + index); the
+	 * comparison against the physical one (7.1 semantics) made ALL
+	 * planes return here and left the RCQ pool without OVL/BLD (green).
+	 */
 	if (layer->type != SUN8I_LAYER_TYPE_UI ||
-	    layer->channel != SUN55I_DE_OVL_UI_PHYS_CHN)
+	    layer->channel != SUN55I_DE_OVL_UI_LOGIC_CHN)
 		return;
 
 	if (!state->crtc || !state->visible || !fb) {
